(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:actor/wave 3), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-concrete-pour :execute-concrete-pour-directly :perform-concrete-placement-directly :finalize-concrete-finishing :override-site-safety-officer :bypass-safety-officer-signoff)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/related (vector "adr-2607121000-cloud-itonami-global-isic-isco-reverse-toposort-plan" "adr-2607152500-cloud-itonami-wave4-rollout-start-amendment")), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "proceed with the concrete pour" "finalize the concrete pour" "finalize the pour" "finalize the finishing work" "authorize the concrete pour" "override the site safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override the site safety officer")), (:adr/id 2799007114), (:actor/domain :construction/concrete-placement-coordination), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :no-client :op-not-allowlisted :no-actuation :scope-exclusion :unknown-site :site-wrong-client :site-not-verified :unknown-worker :worker-wrong-client :worker-not-verified)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "7114"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799007114: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7114 Concrete Placers, Concrete Finishers and Related Workers job-site scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7114\n-- Concrete Placers, Concrete Finishers and Related Workers** only. The\noccupation-actor track is currently working Wave3 (production/trades);\nISCO Wave0/Wave1 are both 100% complete. This is a retry: a prior\nattempt at this exact task was cut off early with no repository\ncreated; this session started clean.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7114\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone (with the `kotoba-lang/technology`\nsibling present at the correct `../technology` relative path) before\nany work began: `clojure -M -e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println\n(kotoba.occupation/get-occupation \\\"7114\\\"))\"` returned `{:id 7114,\n:name Concrete Placers, Concrete Finishers and Related Workers,\n:maturity :spec, :required-technologies [:robotics :identity\n:audit-ledger], :optional-technologies [], :operating-states [:intake\n:propose :approve :execute :audit]}` -- an exact `:name` match, no\nmismatch, confirming the premise. No repository existed at\n`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7114` (`gh api` 404 confirmed before\nscaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry edit promote the\n`7114` entry to `:implemented`.\n\n**This actor carries a construction-site physical-safety dimension:\nconcrete placers and finishers pour and finish concrete on active job\nsites, where material handling and pour timing directly affect worker\nsafety and structural quality, and a poured/finished decision is\neffectively irreversible once made.** A wrongful automated decision\nhere could directly endanger a worker's life or compromise structural\nintegrity. The closed op allowlist therefore must NEVER include any op\nthat directly finalizes a concrete-pour/finishing-execution decision\nor overrides a site-safety officer's judgment -- such a decision must\nalways be a hard, permanent block, never merely an always-escalate op\nand never auto-commit-eligible. This is the same underlying principle\nthe Wave4-amendment ADR (ADR-2607152500) established for decisions\ndirectly touching safety, dignity or subsistence in the human-services\ntrack, and the same shape sibling Wave3 actor cloud-itonami-isco-7121\n(Roofers) applied to its fall-protection safety dimension: the\ncapability to finalize such a decision must be structurally excluded\nfrom the closed op allowlist, not merely gated behind escalation. This\nactor applies that same shape to the concrete-pour-finalization and\nsafety-officer-override dimensions.\n\n**This actor coordinates JOB-SITE SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS ONLY -- it never\nperforms concrete work itself.** It is not an authority to decide when\nor how concrete is poured or finished; it is a coordination layer for\nwork-record logging, crew/pour-timing scheduling, safety-concern\nsurfacing and supply-order coordination, all gated behind an\nindependent governor.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313)\n(Accounting Associate Professionals: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/\n`actor` split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set: README,\nCODE_OF_CONDUCT.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, GOVERNANCE.md, LICENSE\n(AGPL-3.0-or-later), SECURITY.md, docs/business-model.md,\ndocs/operator-guide.md, blueprint.edn), cloned and read in full this\nsession, alongside the already-landed sibling\n`cloud-itonami-isco-7115` (Carpenters and Joiners) for the closer\nconstruction-trades domain shape.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7114` as an OSS\ndocumentation/coordination actor for concrete placers, concrete\nfinishers and related workers, following the same governed-actor\narchitecture as every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this\nfleet: **Concrete Crew Coordination Advisor ⊣ ConcreteCrewGovernor**\non a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a\ndifferent library coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the\nunrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger. All source is portable `.cljc` (no JVM interop); tests\nare `clojure.test` `.clj`, matching the reference repo's own layout.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- task/materials-usage/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task/pour-timing scheduling\n  proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a site-condition/timing/equipment\n  concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit-eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- concrete/materials procurement\n  proposal, escalates above the site's registered cost ceiling\n\nNo op in this allowlist finalizes a concrete-pour/finishing-execution\ndecision or overrides a site-safety officer's judgment -- these\ndecision classes are structurally absent from the allowlist, not\nmerely gated behind escalation.\n\n### Governor HARD checks (`concretecrew.governor`, permanent, never\noverridable by human approval -- a hard block never reaches\n`:request-approval`)\n\n1. **no-client** -- the contractor/crew company must be registered.\n2. **op-not-allowlisted** -- `:op` must be one of the four allowlisted\n   coordination ops; the closed op-allowlist is enforced\n   unconditionally.\n3. **no-actuation** -- proposal `:effect` must be `:propose` (the\n   governor never dispatches hardware and this actor never performs\n   concrete work itself).\n4. **scope-exclusion** -- a proposal whose text content (rationale/\n   task/concern/progress fields) would finalize a concrete-pour/\n   finishing-execution decision, or override a site-safety officer's\n   judgment, is a HARD, PERMANENT block, evaluated unconditionally,\n   independent of `:op`, confidence or stake -- a second, independent\n   line of defense on top of the closed op-allowlist in case a future\n   op or a manipulated text field tries to smuggle such an instruction\n   through an otherwise-allowed op.\n5. **unknown-site / site-wrong-client** -- a proposal must cite a\n   REGISTERED site belonging to this client.\n6. **site-not-verified** -- the cited site must be INDEPENDENTLY\n   VERIFIED (`:verified?` true, e.g. a site-safety officer's\n   inspection sign-off) -- a site record merely existing is not\n   enough.\n7. **unknown-worker / worker-wrong-client / worker-not-verified**\n   (crew operations only) -- a `:schedule-crew-operation` proposal\n   must cite a REGISTERED, independently verified worker belonging to\n   this client.\n\n### Escalation gates, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (`concretecrew.governor/always-escalate-ops`). This is\n  the ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a site-condition/\n  timing/equipment concern -- it never resolves the concern itself.\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds the\n  site's registered `:max-supply-cost` -- always needs human sign-off,\n  independent of confidence (inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-at-exact-supply-cost-ceiling-boundary`; per-site registered\n  ceiling, not a single global constant, since different sites may\n  have different procurement authority).\n- advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` (0.6) also escalates,\n  for any op.\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as bare nouns (e.g.\n\"pour\", \"safety\", \"concrete\") can accidentally match inside the mock\nadvisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this risk is especially\nsharp here because this actor's ENTIRE domain routinely mentions\n\"pour\" (pour-timing scheduling) and \"safety\" (`:flag-safety-concern`\nitself, and its default rationale text). `concretecrew.governor/\nscope-exclusion-phrases` is phrased exclusively as finalization/\nexecution ACTION PHRASES (e.g. \"proceed with the concrete pour\",\n\"finalize the concrete pour\", \"override the site safety officer's\njudgment\"), never bare nouns, and `concretecrew.governor-test/\ndefault-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion` is a\ndedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed allowlist,\ndriven through the default mock advisor against realistic requests\nthat deliberately mention \"pour\" and \"safety\" in their bare-noun\nform (a `:log-work-record` task \"pour-timing update for footing\npour\", a `:flag-safety-concern` concern \"site safety inspection\npending before pour\"), never trips the scope-exclusion guard. Three\ncompanion tests (`hard-on-scope-exclusion-finalize-pour`,\n`hard-on-scope-exclusion-override-safety-officer`,\n`scope-exclusion-not-overridable-by-high-confidence-or-allowlisted-op`)\nconfirm the actual forbidden action phrases DO trip it -- including at\nconfidence 1.0 on an otherwise-allowlisted op, proving the block is\nnot merely a confidence-based escalation -- and\n`holds-a-request-with-scope-excluded-task` in `actor_test.clj`\nconfirms the full actor graph resolves such an attempt straight to\n`:hold` (a finish point, never `:request-approval`) with no record\ncommitted.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7114\" ...}` entry promoted\n  from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id` set to\n  the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7114` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7114`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit to account for concurrent sibling landings in this\n  same batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 25 tests, 55 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a fresh clone of the pushed repository (no mojibake found in\n  the Japanese governor-rule detail strings).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely\n  via the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent\n  with sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`) -- a single-entity EDN vector with an\n  `:adr/body` string blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n- Full doc set published: README.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md,\n  CONTRIBUTING.md, GOVERNANCE.md, SECURITY.md, LICENSE\n  (AGPL-3.0-or-later, byte-identical to the `cloud-itonami-isco-3313`\n  reference's LICENSE text), docs/business-model.md,\n  docs/operator-guide.md, blueprint.edn.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-concrete-pour-completion` that\n  is merely gated behind `always-escalate-ops` (the shape\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`):\n  rejected outright per the task's explicit construction-site-safety\n  guidance and the `ADR-2607152500`/`cloud-itonami-isco-7121`\n  precedent -- an always-escalate op still means the *capability* to\n  finalize a concrete-pour/finishing-execution decision exists in the\n  code path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision\n  that can directly endanger a worker's life or compromise structural\n  integrity, and is effectively irreversible once made, the capability\n  itself must not exist in the allowlist at all.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"pour\" \"safety\"\n  \"concrete\"]`): rejected per the fleet-known self-trip bug class --\n  this actor's entire domain routinely mentions pour-timing and safety\n  concerns as ordinary, unavoidable vocabulary (`:flag-safety-concern`\n  itself contains \"safety\"), so bare nouns would self-trip on\n  essentially every legitimate proposal.\n- Requiring `:verified?` only at registration time (i.e. treating any\n  registered site/worker record as sufficient): rejected -- the task's\n  explicit requirement is that a record be \"independently verified\",\n  not merely registered, so `:verified?` is modeled as a distinct\n  boolean set only by a separate verification step (e.g. a\n  site-safety officer's sign-off), and the governor hard-blocks a\n  registered-but-unverified site or worker exactly like an unknown\n  one.\n- A single global cost-threshold constant for supply-order escalation\n  (the `cloud-itonami-isco-7121` shape): rejected in favor of a\n  per-site registered `:max-supply-cost` ceiling, since different job\n  sites may legitimately have different procurement authority/budget,\n  and a single global constant would either be too permissive for\n  small sites or too restrictive for large ones.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607121000 (governing plan, wave taxonomy and reverse-\n  topological ordering, unchanged)\n- ADR-2607152500 (Wave4 rollout amendment; precedent for structurally\n  excluding safety/dignity/subsistence-adjacent finalization decisions\n  from the closed op allowlist, applied here to construction-site\n  physical safety)\n- `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313` (module-shape reference,\n  independently re-tested)\n- `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7115` (Carpenters and Joiners,\n  closer construction-trades domain reference)\n- `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7121` (Roofers, closest sibling\n  precedent for the hard-scope-exclusion + per-domain self-trip-guard\n  shape)\n- skill `build-actor` (advisor/governor/StateGraph/audit-ledger actor\n  pattern)"), (:adr/date "2026-07-17"), (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order :per-site-registered-max-supply-cost}"), (:test/counts "{:total 25, :assertions 55, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "Concrete Crew Scheduling & Logistics Coordination Service"), (:db/id -1), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :site-verification :worker-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-order-cost-threshold-escalation :always-escalate-safety-concern)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7114"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7114"), (:adr/scope (vector "cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7114" "kotoba-lang/occupation")), (:test/simulator :concretecrew.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7114 — Concrete Placers, Concrete Finishers and Related Workers Job-Site Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000 2607152500)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7114)))
